{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HGJx4bTBpFRYJ8uWfRNrJX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc step hr target units bpm %lthr zone API format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/24\"},{\"title\":\"intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/9\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725\"},{\"title\":\"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return the official intervals.icu API documentation for `workout_doc`, so these findings come from forum posts and third-party docs and should be checked against the API docs.\n\n- **Units:** Forum examples show HR targets as zone numbers (`hr_zone`) and as LTHR percentages, and power as `%ftp` or `power_zone` ([forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/24)). One user reported that a `Z2` step in an HR-based workout could come out as a power target, because the athlete's default sport setting decides which metric applies ([forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/9)).\n- **Range tolerance:** Fixed HR targets are expanded into a range by default, with the developer saying the default is 1.5% for HR. You can override this with an `hrRange` query parameter, and setting it to 0 turns the range off ([API forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)).\n- **Pace and LTHR:** The same developer added `lthr`, `threshold_pace` and `pace_units` fields to `workout_doc` ([API forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)). Another thread notes that HR targets are sent to devices as a percentage of LTHR so that workouts can be shared between users ([Garmin thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157)).\n- **Text syntax:** A third-party Intervals.icu cycling syntax guide lists percent-of-FTP and watt targets, with cadence and ramp options ([cycling syntax](https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md)). I did not find an equivalent HR text-syntax reference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"728161cf-2dd2-441c-95bc-910fcdf33026","uuid":"c6063e8a-74d7-43f9-87ac-5d27098f505a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:54:28.290Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc step hr target units bpm %lthr zone API format","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DC5ZvGBhtNSS9idv6BX2Rh","content":[{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/24"},{"title":"intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/9"},{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725"},{"title":"Building workout using zone number instead of percentage range","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157"}]},"The search didn't return the official intervals.icu API documentation for `workout_doc`, so these findings come from forum posts and third-party docs and should be checked against the API docs.\n\n- **Units:** Forum examples show HR targets as zone numbers (`hr_zone`) and as LTHR percentages, and power as `%ftp` or `power_zone` ([forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/24)). One user reported that a `Z2` step in an HR-based workout could come out as a power target, because the athlete's default sport setting decides which metric applies ([forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/building-workout-using-zone-number-instead-of-percentage-range/4725/9)).\n- **Range tolerance:** Fixed HR targets are expanded into a range by default, with the developer saying the default is 1.5% for HR. You can override this with an `hrRange` query parameter, and setting it to 0 turns the range off ([API forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)).\n- **Pace and LTHR:** The same developer added `lthr`, `threshold_pace` and `pace_units` fields to `workout_doc` ([API forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389)). Another thread notes that HR targets are sent to devices as a percentage of LTHR so that workouts can be shared between users ([Garmin thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157)).\n- **Text syntax:** A third-party Intervals.icu cycling syntax guide lists percent-of-FTP and watt targets, with cadence and ramp options ([cycling syntax](https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md)). I did not find an equivalent HR text-syntax reference."],"durationSeconds":6.295250083000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HGJx4bTBpFRYJ8uWfRNrJX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AwfFqvdCj2zkj8yY9mh73i","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout syntax heart rate target absolute bpm range Garmin export zone\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090\"},{\"title\":\"forum.intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/981\"},{\"title\":\"Syncing both pace and heart rate to Garmin Connect workout\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/syncing-both-pace-and-heart-rate-to-garmin-connect-workout/67330/4\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Workout Builder Syntax Quick Guide\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-syntax-quick-guide/123701\"},{\"title\":\"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163?page=58\"},{\"title\":\"forum.intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/no-pace-targets-on-apple-watch-after-syncing-workout-companion-v3-testflight-build-30/125010\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum posts rather than official documentation, so treat these as user reports.\n\n- **Syntax:** The community syntax cheat sheet lists heart rate targets as a percent of max HR, a percent of threshold HR, or a named zone. Heart rate: Percent of max HR: 70% HR, 75-80% HR; Percent of threshold HR: 95% LTHR, 90-95% LTHR; HR zones: Z2 HR, Z2-Z3 HR. It does not list a plain bpm range in text. Absolute bpm does appear in the API: one bug report shows an HR step with start and end values and a units field set to bpm, and it is described as \"- 60m 122-147bpm Z2 endurance\". Another user's workout also shows \"2km Z2 HR (144-152bpm)\".\n\n- **Garmin export:** A bug report says that after Edge 840 firmware 30.18, the Edge now displays the workout's lower HR bound as bpm_value × HRmax / 100. This would turn an absolute bpm target into a percent of max HR on the device. The same report says that all public export endpoints strip HR-bpm targets entirely when downloading a .zwo file. This is one user's investigation and I could not confirm it elsewhere.\n\n- **Sync limitations:** Another thread notes that if a workout only consists of HR or Pace targets then the output from intervals.icu syncs as expected - any combination thereafter and only a single target type is generated.\n\n- **Unresolved case:** A coach asking about a 130–140 bpm target for an athlete without configured zones was worried that LTHR-based percentages would map to different bpm on the Garmin. The results do not include an answer to that question.\n\nGiven the firmware report, check the bpm range on the device before relying on it, especially after a firmware update.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"728161cf-2dd2-441c-95bc-910fcdf33026","uuid":"5455f8d2-468f-48a5-93a4-792969d186d4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:54:30.357Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout syntax heart rate target absolute bpm range Garmin export zone","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019dEAnmp4xSnpYxHLUPduU9","content":[{"title":"HR target workouts broken on Edge 840 firmware ≥30.18 — interpreted as %HRmax instead of bpm","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-workouts-broken-on-edge-840-firmware-30-18-interpreted-as-hrmax-instead-of-bpm/130090"},{"title":"forum.intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/981"},{"title":"Syncing both pace and heart rate to Garmin Connect workout","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/syncing-both-pace-and-heart-rate-to-garmin-connect-workout/67330/4"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Workout Builder Syntax Quick Guide","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-syntax-quick-guide/123701"},{"title":"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096"},{"title":"Workout builder","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163?page=58"},{"title":"forum.intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/no-pace-targets-on-apple-watch-after-syncing-workout-companion-v3-testflight-build-30/125010"},{"title":"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685"}]},"The search turned up forum posts rather than official documentation, so treat these as user reports.\n\n- **Syntax:** The community syntax cheat sheet lists heart rate targets as a percent of max HR, a percent of threshold HR, or a named zone. Heart rate: Percent of max HR: 70% HR, 75-80% HR; Percent of threshold HR: 95% LTHR, 90-95% LTHR; HR zones: Z2 HR, Z2-Z3 HR. It does not list a plain bpm range in text. Absolute bpm does appear in the API: one bug report shows an HR step with start and end values and a units field set to bpm, and it is described as \"- 60m 122-147bpm Z2 endurance\". Another user's workout also shows \"2km Z2 HR (144-152bpm)\".\n\n- **Garmin export:** A bug report says that after Edge 840 firmware 30.18, the Edge now displays the workout's lower HR bound as bpm_value × HRmax / 100. This would turn an absolute bpm target into a percent of max HR on the device. The same report says that all public export endpoints strip HR-bpm targets entirely when downloading a .zwo file. This is one user's investigation and I could not confirm it elsewhere.\n\n- **Sync limitations:** Another thread notes that if a workout only consists of HR or Pace targets then the output from intervals.icu syncs as expected - any combination thereafter and only a single target type is generated.\n\n- **Unresolved case:** A coach asking about a 130–140 bpm target for an athlete without configured zones was worried that LTHR-based percentages would map to different bpm on the Garmin. The results do not include an answer to that question.\n\nGiven the firmware report, check the bpm range on the device before relying on it, especially after a firmware update."],"durationSeconds":8.118763625,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AwfFqvdCj2zkj8yY9mh73i","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
